{"results":[{"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/endangered-threatened-species","final_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/endangered-threatened-species","title":"Suggested Search - Endangered & Threatened Species","description":"The Endangered Species Act is designed to protect critically imperiled species from extinction as a consequence of economic growth and development. The Fish and Wildlife Service and the National Oceanographic and Atmospheric Administration have primary responsibility to regulate in this area....","language":"en","text":"Legal Status\n\nThis site displays a prototype of a “Web 2.0” version of the daily\nFederal Register. It is not an official legal edition of the Federal\nRegister, and does not replace the official print version or the official\nelectronic version on GPO’s govinfo.gov.\n\nThe documents posted on this site are XML renditions of published Federal\nRegister documents. Each document posted on the site includes a link to the\ncorresponding official PDF file on govinfo.gov. This prototype edition of the\ndaily Federal Register on FederalRegister.gov will remain an unofficial\ninformational resource until the Administrative Committee of the Federal\nRegister (ACFR) issues a regulation granting it official legal status.\nFor complete information about, and access to, our official publications\nand services, go to\nAbout the Federal Register\non NARA's archives.gov.\n\nThe OFR/GPO partnership is committed to presenting accurate and reliable\nregulatory information on FederalRegister.gov with the objective of\nestablishing the XML-based Federal Register as an ACFR-sanctioned\npublication in the future. While every effort has been made to ensure that\nthe material on FederalRegister.gov is accurately displayed, consistent with\nthe official SGML-based PDF version on govinfo.gov, those relying on it for\nlegal research should verify their results against an official edition of\nthe Federal Register. Until the ACFR grants it official status, the XML\nrendition of the daily Federal Register on FederalRegister.gov does not\nprovide legal notice to the public or judicial notice to the courts.\n\nLegal Status\n\n# Suggested Search\n\nEnter a search term or FR citation e.g.\n88 FR 382\n30 FR 7878\n2024-13208\nUSDA\n09/05/24\nRULE\n0503-AA39\nSORN\n\nChoosing an item from\nfull text search results\nwill bring you to those results. Pressing enter in the search box\nwill also bring you to search results.\nChoosing an item from\nsuggestions\nwill bring you directly to the content.\n\nBackground and more details are available in the\n*Search & Navigation*\nguide.\n\n# Endangered & Threatened Species\n\nThe Endangered Species Act is designed to protect critically imperiled species from extinction as a consequence of economic growth and development. The Fish and Wildlife Service and the National Oceanographic and Atmospheric Administration have primary responsibility to regulate in this area. This search may also include related documents from other agencies.\n\nShowing 1-20 of\n30,000+ results\nsince 1994.\nView\nmore results.\n\nView more\nEnvironment\nsearches.\n\n* by the Maritime Administration\n  on 11/05/2026.\n\n  This document proposes procedures for the processing of applications for the licensing of deepwater ports. The proposed rule reflects the transfer of deepwater port license application processing management under the Deepwater Port Act from the United States Coast Guard (USCG) to MARAD. Pursuant to the National Defense Authorization Act for...\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 11/05/2026.\n* by the Fish and Wildlife Service\n  on 11/04/2026.\n\n  In accordance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, we, the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (Service), are proposing to revise an existing information collection.\n* by the Federal Highway Administration\n  on 11/02/2026.\n\n  This notice announces actions taken by the FHWA, on behalf of the Nebraska Department of Transportation and Iowa Department of Transportation, that are final. The action(s) relate to the Decatur Bridge Project, located in Burt County, Nebraska and Monona County, Iowa. Those actions grant licenses, permits, and approvals for the project. The...\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 11/02/2026.\n\n  The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration is initiating a comprehensive review of the Gray's Reef National Marine Sanctuary management plan, to evaluate progress toward implementing the goals of the sanctuary and to revise the management plan as necessary to fulfill the purposes and policies of the National Marine Sanctuaries Act. NOAA...\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/30/2026.\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/30/2026.\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/30/2026.\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/29/2026.\n\n  Notice is hereby given that NMFS received three Hatchery and Genetic Management Plans (HGMPs) for hatchery programs rearing and releasing fall-run chum salmon in the Skagit River basin. The plans describe hatchery programs operated by the Sauk-Suiattle Indian Tribe, Swinomish Indian Tribal Community, Upper Skagit Indian Tribe, and Washington...\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/29/2026.\n\n  In accordance with the regulations implementing the Marine Mammal Protection Act (MMPA), as amended, notification is hereby given that NMFS has issued an incidental harassment authorization (IHA) to PetroMarine Services (PM) to incidentally harass marine mammals incidental to Juneau International Airport (JNU) Rock Dump Fuel Terminal...\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/28/2026.\n\n  NMFS announces the receipt of an application for an exempted fishing permit (EFP) to support cooperative research activities funded by the NOAA RESTORE Science Program to verify, characterize, monitor, and model multi-species fish spawning aggregations in Federal waters of the Gulf of America (Gulf). This notice gives the public an opportunity...\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/28/2026.\n* by the Air Force Department\n  on 10/28/2026.\n\n  The Department of the Air Force (DAF) is issuing this Notice of Intent (NOI) to prepare an Environmental Impact Statement (EIS) to assess the potential social, economic, and environmental effects associated with conducting aircraft training and exercises at airfields in the Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands (CNMI), including Saipan...\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/27/2026.\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/26/2026.\n\n  This notice advises the public that two direct take permits 1454-3R and 1455-3R have been issued for operation, monitoring, and evaluation of a hatchery program rearing and releasing sockeye salmon in the Snake River basin of Idaho, and that the decision documents are available upon request.\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/22/2026.\n\n  In accordance with the regulations implementing the Marine Mammal Protection Act (MMPA), as amended, notification is hereby given that NMFS has issued a renewal incidental harassment authorization (IHA) to Turnagain Marine Services (TMC) to incidentally harass marine mammals incidental to the Seward Cruise Ship Passenger Dock and Terminal...\n* by the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\n  on 10/22/2026.\n\n  In accordance with regulations implementing the Marine Mammal Protection Act (MMPA) as amended, notification is hereby given that NMFS has issued an incidental harassment authorization (IHA) to the United States Navy (Navy) for authorization to take marine mammals incidental to Year 1 of the Bremerton Waterfront Infrastructure Improvements...\n* by the Ocean Energy Management Bureau\n  on 10/20/2026.\n\n  The Marine Minerals Administration (MMA) will conduct an auction for lease areas offered in the American Samoa Outer Continental Shelf (OCS) Pacific Mineral Lease Sale 1 (Lease Sale PACM-1), in accordance with the Outer Continental Shelf Lands Act (OCSLA), as amended, and its implementing regulations. The Final Leasing Notice (FLN) package for...\n* by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\n  on 10/20/2026.\n\n  The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission proposes to revise its regulations to establish procedures for authorizing activities at liquefied natural gas plants without case-specific authorization orders under sections 3 or 7 of the Natural Gas Act.\n\nShowing 1-20 of\n30,000+ results\nsince 1994.\nView\nmore results.\n\nView more\nEnvironment\nsearches.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":245.62105600489303,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}